From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000008 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 24 Mar 2026 15:49:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] wifi: mt76: mt7996: fix out-of-bounds array access during
 hardware restart

Add mt7996_sta_link() and mt7996_sta_link_protected() inline helpers that
bounds-check the link_id index against IEEE80211_MLD_MAX_NUM_LINKS before
dereferencing msta->link[link_id]. Without this check, a link_id value
from a corrupted or unexpected hardware state could cause an out-of-bounds
access on the link array.

Replace all open-coded rcu_dereference(msta->link[link_id]) and
mt76_dereference(msta->link[link_id], ...) calls with the new helpers
throughout debugfs.c, mac.c, main.c, mcu.c.

Fixes: CVE-2026-23325
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Link: https://patchwork.kernel.org/project/linux-wireless/patch/20260324154904.2555603-1-nbd@nbd.name/
